From b090fcfd59352469de0b9f8039e4e590958de363 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:38:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Pile-On's real month-switch/detail-panel bug and Library
 Configure routing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause found: "pre call sequence" is Pile-On's actual display name
(SKILL_MANIFEST["pile-on"].name === "Pre-Call Sequence") — a different
skill than pre-call-read ("Call Brief"). "All Activity" only exists in
pile-on-pipeline.tsx, confirming it. The month-switch bug report was
about this file all along, not pre-call-read-pipeline.tsx.

pile-on-pipeline.tsx:
- The real bug: `selected` fell back to `filtered.find(id === selectedId)`
  — filtered is the WHOLE engagement's items (loaded once, no per-month
  refetch here, unlike pre-call-read), so a stale selectedId kept
  resolving to last month's item indefinitely once the reset effect
  raced it, which is exactly "the right panel shows something, the left
  [day] list doesn't match." Now only trusts selectedId when it's
  actually in the currently selected day's items.
- rounded-2xl -> rounded-lg, rounded-xl -> rounded-md across toolbar/
  panels/calendar grid, matching the "less rounded" ask.
- Swept the remaining no-ambient-glow surface-glass-1/2 fills (this
  file was never touched by the earlier transparency passes) and two
  bg-zinc-100/80 header-strip fills to bg-transparent + border.

worker-card.tsx: Configure for any worker without a "hinges panel"
(Pile-On's hasHingesPanel is false) linked to the bare
/dashboard/engagements/{id} page instead of that worker's own page —
exactly the "Configure takes me to engagements id" report. Now routes
through workerPrimaryHref like every other "go manage this skill" link
in the app.

Note: Pile-On still has no way to *re*-configure (change SMS/ad-data
platform) after initial enable — EnablePileOnModal is enable-only, adds
no reading of current values, and isn't wired to any page's own
Configure entry point. That's a real, separate feature to build if
wanted, not something this routing fix can paper over.

